the banner saga will take you on an  immersive journey where your choices  directly affect how your personal story  unfolds in this tutorial we'll be going  over the basics of combat which will  cover your strategies and prepare you  for the battle and your tactics in the  field combat in the banner saga is split  between battle and walls a battle is a  small-scale fight where only your party  of six are affected a war occurs when  your caravan meets a large number of  enemies when this happens you will be  presented with a summary of the pending  situation along with several options of  how to proceed your choices here will  affect how many of your side's survive  the fight and your choices at this stage  will also affect how difficult the  combat is before you take part in any  battle of war you have to choose which  six heroes to take with you you can  choose any hero from your entire roster  and you can mix and match any  combination of class you might have  heroes can become injured if they're not  unconscious in battles so you'll have to  rest them for a number of days before  their full strength again before  choosing a hero make sure you are  familiar with their stats armor strength  willpower exertion and break armor  blocks damage your strength minus their  armor equals damage strength is both  damage and health if it drops to zero  the unit full unconscious willpower  expect to move further hit harder  and perform abilities but does not  replenish during combat once you've  spent all your world car you will not be  able to use a hero special ability  exertion is the amount of willpower you  can use on any given direction brake is  the amount of direct damage you can  naturally due to an enemy's armor lastly  make sure that you have promoted or  applied extra stat points to any  qualifying hero and equip any passive  ability enhancing items that you might  have picked up or bought along the way  it's also useful to become familiar with  each heroes special active ability and  how it works in combination with the  other heroes in the party when used in  unison these can turn the tide of battle  in an instant once you have assembled  your heroes you are ready to jump into  battle the banner saga embraces  turn-based tactical combat which means  each unit takes a turn to make their  move similar to a game of chess the  order in which the units will make their  move is shown in the bottom left side of  your screen in the initiative bar you  can hit tab at the beginning of a battle  to show how the enemy stats compared to  your stats armor strength and willpower  are showing when it's your turn you can  move use mobility attack or rest if you  are in range and you choose to attack  your enemy you can either attack their  strengths or break their armor the week  of their armor they're more susceptible  there will be when this rope is directly  willpower can be used in a battle to  boost actions for example if you are  just out of range to make an attack on  an enemy you can use willpower to move  within range or you can add willpower to  boost an actual attack on ice our mobile  strength  well pad boos are a limited resource  however and are determined by your  exertions fat so use it wisely this  completes your rough guide to combat  more details can be learnt in game  during the early tutorial missions to  help you get started on your journey as  you progress and gain experience in  combat you will not only be challenged  more but you will also discover the  deeper strategic combat that is at the  heart of the banner saga to learn more  about the game visit our forums website  and Facebook page
 

